# Copy this file to .env (gitignored, per-machine) and fill in the path
# below to share the Crowdstrike vulnerability history CSV via SharePoint.
#
# 1. Open the SharePoint document library in a browser and click
#    "Sync" (top toolbar) to add it to your OneDrive client.
# 2. In File Explorer, right-click the synced library folder and confirm
#    "Always keep on this device" (NOT "Free up space") - OneDrive's
#    Files On-Demand feature can otherwise leave files as offline
#    placeholders that Docker's bind mount can't read.
# 3. Copy that folder's full local path below (e.g.
#    C:\Users\<you>\LBH Group\Security - Documents\crowdstrike).
#
# Leave unset to keep using the local ./data/crowdstike folder instead
# (each machine keeps its own separate history).
CROWDSTRIKE_HISTORY_DIR=C:\Users\<you>\LBH Group\Security - Documents\crowdstrike
